          "script": "Hook: Show me 2 fingers on your left hand. Now show 3 fingers on your right hand. Count ALL fingers — how many? Five! You just did addition!\n\nStep 1: Addition means PUTTING TOGETHER. When you have some things and get more, you count them all — that's addition! Pick up 2 spoons, then 3 more. Put together. Count: 5! We write 2 + 3 = 5.\n\nStep 2: Try 4 + 1. Take 4 toy cars. Add 1 more. Count: 5! So 4 + 1 = 5.\n\nStep 3: Let your child make one up! Pick objects, make two groups, put together, count.\n\nPitfall: Children count both groups from 1. For 3+2, they say '1,2,3' then '1,2' and say '2'. Teach them to CONTINUE counting: '3...4, 5!'",
